ue_on":null,"closed_at":null},"comments":4,"created_at":"2023-05-12T17:52:06Z","updated_at":"2023-05-12T20:29:53Z","closed_at":"2023-05-12T20:29:52Z","author_association":"NONE","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Describe the bug\n\nThis causes `CreateEnumType` elements to be emitted when creating tables, even though they should not. I believe the fix is as simple as forwarding the `kwarg` from `impl` here: https://github.com/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/blob/rel_1_4_48/lib/sqlalchemy/dialects/postgresql/base.py#L2077-L2090\r\n\r\n\n\n### Optional link from https://docs.sqlalchemy.org which documents the behavior that is expected\n\n_No response_\n\n### SQLAlchemy Version in Use\n\n1.4.25\n\n### DBAPI (i.e. the database driver)\n\npsycopg2\n\n### Database Vendor and Major Version\n\nPostgreSQL 12\n\n### Python Version\n\n3.9\n\n### Operating system\n\nOSX\n\n### To Reproduce\n\n```python\nimport enum\r\n\r\nfrom sqlalchemy import Column\r\nfrom sqlalchemy.dialects.postgresql import ENUM\r\nfrom sqlalchemy.orm import declarative_base\r\n\r\nBase = declarative_base()\r\n\r\nclass Period(enum.Enum):\r\n    MONTH = \"MONTH\"\r\n    QUARTER = \"QUARTER\"\r\n    YEAR = \"YEAR\"\r\n\r\n\r\nclass ModelBase:\r\n    period = Column(\r\n        ENUM(Period, create_type=False),\r\n        primary_key=True,\r\n        nullable=False,\r\n    )\r\n\r\n\r\nclass TestModel(ModelBase, Base):\r\n    __tablename__ = \"test_model\"\r\n\r\n\r\nprint(\r\n    ModelBase.period.type.create_type,\r\n    TestModel.__table__.columns['period'].type.create_type\r\n) # => False True\n```\n\n\n### Error\n\nn/a\n\n### Additional context\n\n_No response_","closed_by":{"login":"sqlalchemy-bot","id":36047385,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MDQ3Mzg1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36047385?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url"